  "body": "Part of #2574 (research answers 5 and 9).\n\nMaintainer request, 2026-11-18, in his words (quoted in #2574):\n> \"It should still run on the same infrastructure of egui, step loader, solidcore etc. etc.. Alot of the basis is already there but it is it's own executable.\"\n\n## Scope\n- `camcraft-sim <file.nc> ...` with no subcommand opens a window (egui, egui-wgpu, winit from the workspace). File open dialogs for the NC file, the `.mch`, the `.cps` and the stock.\n- Play the program on the machine model (#2584) and the stock (`FieldPlay` after #2268): play, pause, step, scrub.\n- A findings list from the checks of #2586. A click on a finding jumps to its NC line and its playback position. A \"not judged\" line is shown, never hidden.\n- An NC text pane with the current line marked.\n- No playback state is saved; there is no document and no undo.\n- The window refuses bad input with a named message and does not panic.\n- Follow `crates/ui/AGENTS.md` for the look where it applies. Screenshots in the PR body.\n\n## Done means\nThe window opens a 3-axis program with its machine and stock, plays it on the generated model, and lists the findings with working line jumps. Frame tests (egui_kittest) pin the labels and the findings list.\n\nDepends on #2586 and #2268.\n",
